Represents each individual product or service line on a Sales Order / Quotation, containing quantity, price, discount, taxes, and delivery information.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Define ordered items with unit price, discounts, and taxes
Trigger stock reservations and deliveries (stock.move)
Calculate line and order totals (subtotal, tax, total)
Support product configurator, upsell, and service hours
Handle partial deliveries and remaining quantities
Sales reporting, margin analysis per line/product
Dropshipping and Make-To-Order flows

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
order_id → sale.order (required, parent)
product_id → product.product, product_uom_qty (float)
price_unit (monetary), discount (float %)
tax_id (Many2many to account.tax)
qty_delivered, qty_invoiced, qty_to_invoice
price_reduce (discounted price), margin, purchase_price
commitment_date, name (description)

Critical Hooks: onchange_product_id, _compute_amount, _compute_margin, _prepare_procurement_values, _compute_qty_delivered
Security: Inherited from parent sale.order

RAG Routing Keywords:
sales order line, SO line, quotation line, sale line, customer order line, sales order detail, ordered quantity, sales discount line, delivered quantity, invoiced quantity, sale product line, margin line
Related Models (most joined):

sale.order (parent)
product.product / product.template
stock.move / stock.picking (deliveries)
account.move.line (invoicing)
res.partner (via order)
uom.uom
account.tax

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
sale.order.line is the child model of sale.order that stores each sold item with product_id, product_uom_qty, price_unit, discount, tax_id, and delivery/invoicing quantities. It drives stock reservation, delivery creation, invoice line generation, margin calculation, and is the core transactional detail used across Sales, Inventory, and Accounting in Odoo.